# ── With Docker (docker compose up) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Nothing is required. To change something, put it in a file named .env (Compose reads that one):
# APP_PORT=3000              the app
# DB_PORT=5432               PostgreSQL, for database tools (change it if you already run PostgreSQL)
# MAIL_UI_PORT=8025          the email inbox (Mailpit)
# MAIL_SMTP_PORT=1025        Mailpit's SMTP, for `npm run dev` outside Docker
# SEED_ON_START=false        don't add the demo data on every start
# WATCH_POLL_INTERVAL_MS=1000   if hot reload misses your edits (some Windows/macOS setups); uses more CPU
# The social sign-in keys below also work there. compose.prod.yaml needs AUTH_SECRET.

# ── Without Docker (npm run dev on your machine) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to .env.local (Next.js and the db:* scripts read it). Never commit real values.
# `make db` (docker compose up -d db mail) starts PostgreSQL and the email inbox with these settings.

# PostgreSQL.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://lumina:lumina@localhost:5432/lumina
# Connections per server process (default 10).
# DATABASE_POOL_MAX=10

# Encrypts two-step verification secrets. Required in production; keep it stable (changing it turns off
# everyone's authenticator app). Generate with: openssl rand -base64 48
# AUTH_SECRET=

# This site's public address. Used in emails, redirects and the social sign-in callback. Set in production.
# APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# The public address for SEO (canonical URLs, sitemap.xml, robots.txt, share images). Read when the app is
# BUILT (it ends up in prerendered HTML); defaults to APP_URL, then localhost. Builds pointing at localhost,
# or with SITE_NOINDEX=true (previews, staging), are kept out of search engines.
# SITE_URL=https://lumina.example
# SITE_NOINDEX=true

# Force Secure cookies on (true) or off (false). Default: on for HTTPS requests.
# COOKIE_SECURE=

# Outgoing email. Without SMTP_URL, emails are printed to the server log (fine for development).
# With `make db`, Mailpit catches them at http://localhost:8025:
# SMTP_URL=smtp://localhost:1025
# Production: SMTP_URL=smtps://user:password@smtp.example.com:465
# MAIL_FROM=Lumina <no-reply@lumina.example>

# Social sign-in: a provider's button appears once its keys are set. Redirect URI for all three:
# <APP_URL>/auth/callback
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID=
# MICROSOFT_CLIENT_SECRET=
# MICROSOFT_TENANT=common
# APPLE_CLIENT_ID=
# APPLE_TEAM_ID=
# APPLE_KEY_ID=
# APPLE_PRIVATE_KEY="-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\n...\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----"

# Integration tests (npm test) use their own database, created automatically:
# TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://lumina:lumina@localhost:5432/lumina_test
